    <header class="site-header"><div class="wrap"><a class="logo" href="/"><img src="/assets/xgl-txt-logo-clean.webp" alt="Expedition Growth Lab" /></a><nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary navigation"><a href="/the-lab">The Lab</a><a href="/command-central">Command Central</a><a class="active" href="/one-rising-sun">One Rising Sun</a><a href="/faq">FAQ</a><a href="/about">About</a><a href="/contact">Contact</a></nav><a class="assessment-cta" href="/assessment">Start Assessment</a><details class="mobile-menu"><summary>Menu</summary><div class="mobile-menu-panel"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/the-lab">The Lab</a><a href="/command-central">Command Central</a><a href="/one-rising-sun">One Rising Sun</a><a href="/faq">FAQ</a><a href="/about">About</a><a href="/contact">Contact</a><a href="/assessment">Start Assessment</a></div></details></div></header>
    <main>
      <section class="hero image-hero" style="background-image:url('/assets/one-rising-sun-hero.webp')"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">The Independent Partnership &amp; Membership Network</div><h1 class="ors-serif" style="font-size:clamp(78px,9vw,128px);line-height:.9;margin:0">One Rising<br />Sun.</h1><p class="hero-copy" style="font-size:20px">A vetted alliance for builders, service providers, product makers, stewards, and community leaders working to make the overland world stronger—not merely louder.</p><a class="button gold" href="/contact" style="margin-top:24px">Begin the Conversation</a></div></section>
      <section class="section cream"><div class="wrap section-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow orange">Why it exists</div><h2 class="section-title">Different roles.<br />One responsibility to the trail.</h2></div><div class="copy">No company builds alone. Products move through suppliers, fabricators, dealers, creators, events, clubs, customers, public lands, and local communities.<br /><br />One Rising Sun connects trustworthy independent operators without reducing partnership to logo placement, referral math, or ceremonial handshakes beside a folding table.</div></div></section>
      <section class="section dark"><div class="wrap"><div class="role-grid"><article class="role"><div class="num">01</div><h3 style="text-transform:none">Utility</h3><p>The relationship must create something genuinely useful.</p></article><article class="role"><div class="num">02</div><h3 style="text-transform:none">Trust</h3><p>We say what we mean, keep our word, and protect the people whose work makes the partnership possible.</p></article><article class="role"><div class="num">03</div><h3 style="text-transform:none">Independence</h3><p>Growth should strengthen good companies without sanding away their identity or handing away their future.</p></article><article class="role"><div class="num">04</div><h3 style="text-transform:none">Community</h3><p>Success should strengthen founders, employees, customers, communities, and the trail itself.</p></article></div></div></section>
      <section class="section cream"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow orange">Membership Registry</div><h2 class="section-title" style="max-width:900px">The first lights are on.</h2><p class="copy" style="max-width:850px;margin-top:30px">Membership is earned through fit, evidence, and accountability. Payment for XGL services does not purchase admission, and One Rising Sun membership does not require becoming an XGL client.</p><div class="ors-member-grid"><article class="ors-member-card"><div class="ors-status">Confirmed founding member</div><h3>Cascadia Trailer &amp; Equipment</h3><div class="ors-member-meta">Reedsport, Oregon · Builder &amp; Field Service</div><p>Custom coach construction, van and RV conversions, service, repair, electrical systems, and practical field support.</p></article><article class="ors-member-card pending"><div class="ors-status pending">Membership pending final agreement</div><h3>Solar Ark Electrical LLC</h3><div class="ors-member-meta">Arizona · Electrical &amp; Solar</div><p>Independent electrical and solar capability grounded in engineering knowledge, hands-on work, education, and accountable service.</p></article></div><div class="ors-principle"><strong>Cooperate where scale helps. Remain independent where identity matters.</strong><br />The network will include client and non-client members, service partners, product partners, development and education partners, community partners, and Stewards. Every lane carries its own agreement, responsibilities, and scope of authority.</div></div></section>
      <section class="section dark"><div class="wrap" style="max-width:900px"><div class="eyebrow gray">Partnership Paths</div><h2 class="section-title">Built around shared work.</h2><p class="copy">Relationships may include builder support, vetted field service, product and equipment capability, systems collaboration, referrals, co-created intelligence, event programs, research, education, community service, or other work that becomes valuable because the right people chose to build it together.<br /><br />The shape follows the opportunity. The standards do not bend to fit the opportunity.</p><a class="button" href="/contact" style="margin-top:24px">Bring Us the Possibility</a><div class="ors-reference"><p>Reference framework: 57 founding instruments covering charter, membership, agreements, governance, and compliance. Working drafts require counsel review before execution.</p><a href="/one-rising-sun/founding-documents">Founding documents →</a></div></div></section>
